1 OCCU Biskop, författare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Olof Bjurbäck , born 29 October 1750 in Lungsund parish , Värmland County, died 18 April 1829 in Karlstad city parish , Värmland County,  was a Swedish bishop , author and translator . He was the son of the hammers
2 CONC mith Jonas Olsson and Maria Svensdotter Bock. In 1811 Bjurbäck married Maria Lundgren.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born at Bjurbäck's mill in Lungsund parish and took his surname after his birthplace. From a couple of events in Bjurbäck's early years, his relatives assumed that he would become something great. When he was baptized, he w
2 CONC as carelessly dropped on the floor, but was picked up without any signs of injury, and a few years later he fell unnoticed from the vehicle during a move and was found a couple of hours later, in an undisturbed sleep on the highwa
2 CONC y, in front of Kil Church , where he later became pastor as bishop of Karlstad .
2 CONT Through the support of benefactors he was given the opportunity to study. At Uppsala University , where he enrolled as a student in 1770, he received a philosophical degree in 1774 and was ordained a priest in 1775. Despite his le
2 CONC arning and excellent qualities, he did not receive an ordinary promotion until the age of 37, when he was appointed (1787) as eloquent lecturer in Karlstad. In 1801 he exchanged this teaching position for the position of vicar in 
2 CONC the Filipstad parish , which he only held until 1803, when he became bishop of the Karlstad diocese .
2 CONT Bjurbäck is considered one of the foremost representatives of Lockeanism of his time . Already during his studies in Uppsala , he became interested in philosophy , where he enjoyed Christiernin's personal guidance. Even during his
2 CONC  teaching career, Bjurbäck distinguished himself for his diverse scientific interests. As a priest , he cared for his congregations with great zeal and worked for an orderly provision for the poor and the upliftment of the working
2 CONC  classes. The same philanthropic spirit also permeated his activities as a member of parliament (1809–1815).
2 CONT
2 CONT A chronic illness constantly plagued him, along with the notion that he was not conscientiously fulfilling his position, and only the strong urgings of his friends prevented him from resigning his position. Bjurbäck donated part o
2 CONC f his unusually rich book collection to the Uppsala University Library .
2 CONT
2 CONT Bjurbäck was a diligent scholar and scholar , and published a large number of occasional writings on church and political subjects, as well as translations of Shakespeare's Hamlet (1820) and Schiller's Cabal and Love (1821), and i
2 CONC n his manuscript , translations of King Lear , Klopstock's Messiah , Ossian's Songs , and several other works are preserved . His printed writings testify to his versatile learning.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Verksam i Karlstad stift.
